.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt HIER 7
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm hier
.Nd layout of the file system
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This page describes where things are kept on an OxideBSD system, and why.
The layout follows the one the BSDs share; where OxideBSD differs, the entry
says so.
The source tree mirrors it: a program built from
.Pa bin/ ,
.Pa sbin/ ,
.Pa usr.bin/
or
.Pa usr.sbin/
is installed in the directory of the same name.
.Ss Choosing a directory for a program
Two questions decide where a program goes, in this order:
.Bl -enum -offset indent
.It
Does repairing the system in single-user mode, with only the root file
system, need it?
If so, it goes in
.Pa /bin
or
.Pa /sbin ;
otherwise in
.Pa /usr/bin
or
.Pa /usr/sbin .
.It
Is it for administering the system rather than using it?
If so, it goes in one of the
.Pa sbin
directories.
.El
.Pp
The programs in
.Pa /bin
and
.Pa /sbin
are statically linked, as on
.Ox ,
so that a broken shared library cannot take away the tools for repairing the
system.
Everything under
.Pa /usr
is dynamically linked.
.Ss The directories
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/share/"
.It Pa /
The root directory.
.It Pa /bin
Commands everyone needs, in single-user mode too.
OxideBSD keeps more here than
.Fx
does:
.Xr vi 1 ,
.Xr grep 1 ,
.Xr sed 1 ,
.Xr tar 1
and
.Xr gzip 1
are what a repair actually uses, so they are here, not in
.Pa /usr/bin .
.It Pa /dev
Devices: a
.Xr devfs 4
file system, made anew at every boot from the kernel's devices and
.Xr devfs.conf 5 .
.Pa /dev/log
is the local socket
.Xr syslogd 8
reads;
.Pa /dev/klog
is the kernel's message buffer,
.Xr klog 4 .
.It Pa /etc
Configuration of the local system.
.Bl -tag -width "newsyslog.conf.d/"
.It Pa defaults/
The defaults the files beside it override:
.Pa rc.conf .
Never edited.
.It Pa pam.d/
PAM policies, one file per service.
.It Pa rc , rc.shutdown , rc.subr
The boot and shutdown scripts and their shared functions;
.Xr rc 8 ,
.Xr rc.subr 8 .
.It Pa rc.conf
Which services run and how;
.Xr rc.conf 5 .
.It Pa rc.d/
One script per service, ordered by
.Xr rcorder 8 .
.It Pa ssl/
OpenSSL's directory:
.Pa openssl.cnf ,
and the trusted certificate authorities as
.Pa cert.pem
and as links in
.Pa certs/ ,
with the distrusted ones in
.Pa untrusted/ ,
all maintained by
.Xr certctl 8 .
.It Pa syslog.conf , syslog.d/
.Xr syslog.conf 5 .
.It Pa newsyslog.conf , newsyslog.conf.d/
.Xr newsyslog.conf 5 .
.It Pa localtime
The system's time zone, a symbolic link to a file in
.Pa /usr/share/zoneinfo ;
see
.Xr tzsetup 8 .
.It Pa master.passwd , passwd , group
Accounts and groups;
.Xr passwd 5 ,
.Xr pwd_mkdb 8 .
.El
.Pp
Also here:
.Xr devfs.conf 5 ,
.Xr gettytab 5 ,
.Xr login.conf 5 ,
.Xr man.conf 5 ,
.Xr sysctl.conf 5 ,
.Xr ttys 5 ,
.Pa hosts ,
.Pa resolv.conf
and
.Pa motd .
.It Pa /home
Users' home directories.
.It Pa /lib
The dynamic linker and the libraries every dynamically linked program needs,
where those programs look for them:
.Pa libc.so ,
musl's C library, which is also the dynamic linker
.Pa ld-musl-x86_64.so.1 ;
and
.Pa libgcc_s.so.1 ,
the unwinder.
.It Pa /proc
Process information, made up by the file system when it is read.
.It Pa /sbin
Commands needed to boot, repair, configure and shut down the system,
usually by the superuser.
.It Pa /tmp
Temporary files.
Anyone may create files here; only their owner may remove them.
It may be a memory file system; see
.Va tmpmfs
in
.Xr rc.conf 5 .
.It Pa /usr
Everything not needed in single-user mode.
.Bl -tag -width "libexec/"
.It Pa bin/
Every other command.
.It Pa games/
Games.
.It Pa include/
C and C++ headers: the C library's, libc++'s in
.Pa c++/v1 ,
and the target's own in
.Pa x86_64-unknown-oxidebsd-musl/ .
.It Pa lib/
Every other library, static and shared, and links to
.Pa /lib Ns 's
under the names the linker looks for.
.Pa clang/23/
holds Clang's headers and runtime;
.Pa ossl-modules/
OpenSSL's loadable providers.
.It Pa libexec/
Programs other programs run, not users:
.Xr getty 8 .
.It Pa local/
Software added to the system that is not part of it:
.Pa bin/ , sbin/ , etc/rc.d/
and so on, as under
.Pa /usr .
Nothing in the base system is installed here.
.It Pa sbin/
Every other administration command, and the daemons.
.It Pa share/
Data that does not depend on the machine:
.Bl -tag -width "zoneinfo/"
.It Pa certs/
The certificate authorities the system ships, from Mozilla's list, in
.Pa trusted/
and
.Pa untrusted/ .
.It Pa man/
Manual pages, and their index
.Pa oxdoc.db ;
.Xr man 1 ,
.Xr makewhatis 8 .
.It Pa mk/
.Xr make 1 Ns 's
include files.
.It Pa terminfo/
Terminal descriptions.
.It Pa zoneinfo/
Time zones.
.El
.It Pa src/
Source code.
.It Pa tests/
Test programs; not on anyone's
.Ev PATH .
.El
.It Pa /var
Files that change while the system runs.
.Bl -tag -width "mail/"
.It Pa log/
Logs, written by
.Xr syslogd 8
and rotated by
.Xr newsyslog 8 .
.It Pa mail/
Mailboxes.
.It Pa run/
Process ID files and other state of running programs, emptied at boot.
.El
.El
.Ss Search path
Every login gets the same
.Ev PATH ,
from
.Xr login.conf 5 :
.Pp
.Dl /sbin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/games:~/bin
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr login.conf 5 ,
.Xr rc.conf 5 ,
.Xr rc 8
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
manual page appeared in
.At v7 .
OxideBSD's is modelled on the BSDs'.
.Sh CAVEATS
The root directory also holds files for the test suites
.Pf ( Pa /posix-tests , /sh-smoke , /ninja-demo
and a few sources).
They belong in
.Pa /usr/tests
and will move there.
